"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-7260-7504"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "AI R&D Center, Seegene Medical Foundation, Seoul, Korea."}, {"affiliation": "Department of Medical Sciences, Graduate School, The Catholic University of Korea, Seoul, Korea."}]}}, {"fullName": "Jeong WC", "lastName": "Jeong", "firstName": "Won Chan", "initials": "WC", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0009-0008-1931-5957"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "AI R&D Center, Seegene Medical Foundation, Seoul, Korea."}]}}, {"fullName": "Hwang Y", "lastName": "Hwang", "firstName": "Yuri", "initials": "Y", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-2433-4991"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "AI R&D Center, Seegene Medical Foundation, Seoul, Korea."}]}}, {"fullName": "Hwang G", "lastName": "Hwang", "firstName": "Gisu", "initials": "G", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-1046-9286"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "AI R&D Center, Seegene Medical Foundation, Seoul, Korea."}]}}, {"fullName": "Kim K", "lastName": "Kim", "firstName": "Kyungeun", "initials": "K", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-7938-4673"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "AI R&D Center, Seegene Medical Foundation, Seoul, Korea."}, {"affiliation": "Pathology Center, Seegene Medical Foundation, Seoul, Korea."}]}}, {"fullName": "Ko YS", "lastName": "Ko", "firstName": "Young Sin", "initials": "YS", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-1319-4847"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "AI R&D Center, Seegene Medical Foundation, Seoul, Korea."}, {"affiliation": "Pathology Center, Seegene Medical Foundation, Seoul, Korea."}]}}]}, "authorIdList": {"authorId": [{"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-7260-7504"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-7938-4673"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-2433-4991"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-1046-9286"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-1319-4847"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0009-0008-1931-5957"}]}, "dataLinksTagsList": {"dataLinkstag": ["supporting_data"]}, "journalInfo": {"issue": "6", "volume": "89", "journalIssueId": 4307466, "dateOfPublication": "2026 Dec", "monthOfPublication": 12, "yearOfPublication": 2026, "journal": {"medlineAbbreviation": "Histopathology", "title": "Histopathology", "essn": "1365-2559", "issn": "0309-0167", "nlmid": "7704136", "isoabbreviation": "Histopathology"}, "printPublicationDate": "2026-12-01"}, "pubYear": "2026", "pageInfo": "1042-1055", "abstractText": "<h4>Aims</h4>The Updated Sydney System is the most widely used framework for histological grading of gastritis, but complete grading in routine gastric biopsies is time-consuming and subject to interobserver variability. We developed an artificial intelligence (AI) system to support comprehensive and reproducible grading of all five Updated Sydney attributes in gastric biopsies.<h4>Methods and results</h4>We developed SydneyMTL, a weakly supervised multi-task multiple instance learning framework trained on 50,765 whole-slide images from routine practice. The model jointly predicts mononuclear cell infiltration, neutrophil activity, glandular atrophy, intestinal metaplasia and Helicobacter pylori density, with atrophy including a separate not applicable category when muscularis mucosae is absent. Performance was assessed against routine labels from 24 board-certified pathologists and against a consensus-adjudicated Golden dataset. SydneyMTL achieved a mean lenient accuracy of 89.1% across the 24 pathologists, with >80% agreement for 21 of 24 readers on the retrospective dataset. In a two-reader randomized crossover study, AI assistance improved interobserver agreement and reduced review time by 34.2% for complete Updated Sydney grading.<h4>Conclusions</h4>AI can support more reproducible and efficient grading of Updated Sydney histological attributes in gastric biopsies. By combining multi-pathologist validation, consensus-based evaluation and explicit handling of non-assessable atrophy, SydneyMTL provides a clinically realistic decision-support approach for routine digital pathology.", "affiliation": "AI R&D Center, Seegene Medical Foundation, Seoul, Korea.", "publicationStatus": "ppublish", "language": "eng", "pubModel": "Print-Electronic", "pubTypeList": {"pubType": ["research-article", "Validation Study", "Journal Article"]}, "meshHeadingList": {"meshHeading": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Stomach", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "PA", "qualifierName": "pathology"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Gastric Mucosa", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "PA", "qualifierName": "pathology"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Humans"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Helicobacter pylori"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Helicobacter Infections", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "PA", "qualifierName": "pathology"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "descriptorName": "Gastritis", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "DI", "qualifierName": "diagnosis"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "PA", "qualifierName": "pathology"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Observer Variation"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Biopsy"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Reproducibility of Results"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "descriptorName": "Artificial Intelligence"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Multiple-Instance Learning Algorithms"}]}, "keywordList": {"keyword": ["Gastritis", "Digital Pathology", "Multiple Instance Learning", "Updated Sydney System", "Multi‐task Learning"]}, "sub